# Wave W17-Z (Farewell Spring): pool post — a still-pool marker post at the spring pool’s shore: a quiet post with one pale ripple ring held at its foot where the water’s edge meets the grass, marking the lone duck’s pool (design: the pool keeps its posts; no bird is invented — the duck is the design’s, the posts are the kit’s). On fare turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s marker posts by the ripple entire: posts mark a road, this one marks stillness.
